Z||000002||Cooter||07-03-2000||10:54 PM||||I have a set of heads at the machine shop being cut for 1.94 intake and 1.55 exhaust valves. He will use standard SBC valves with the stem ends trimmed to the correct length. By using these more readily available valves, swirl polished and undercut stems were not hard to get. I wonder how my 3.4 will run with these heads???||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||07-03-2000||11:19 PM||||According to my Desktop Dyno simulation you will gain 18 HP at 6000 RPM and 16 FT LB’s of torque at 6000 RPM. You will loose about 1 hp and three FT IB’S of torque at 2000 RPM.||||reg||1
