Z||000007||Phaeton||07-04-2000||04:31 AM||||I had access to a valve grinding machine and no plan for racing or exotic fuel, so.<P>Using a small block chevy swirl polished SS valve set for models I shaped and polished a set of factory valves to match.  I didn't mess with the seat itself, strictly ass-o-meter stuff.  A bargain because it was the price of stock plus my own time, paying a stranger shop rate may be over budget.||||reg||12
Z||000008||HYPTNOTiSE||07-04-2000||11:11 AM||||no offense cooter, but i think you're heads are going to be at the machine shop forever before they get valves that large into the ho-iron heads. Stock is somewhere on the idea of 1.72/1.47 that's .30 difference and that's over 1/4 inch! There's no way, they're simply not enough room.<P>Mike LeCompte||||reg||1
