Z||000012||Cooter||07-04-2000||11:20 PM||||Called the machine shop yesterday- It is dirt track season and big paying customers come before small, time consuming projects. I was reassured that it can be done. The intake valves will be .22 larger (1.72 vs. 1.94) and the exhaust will be .008 larger (1.50 vs. 1.42). The big advantage will be the fact of undercut stems in the bowl area, a professional bowl blend and port match. He can not fit the 1.55 exhaust because they are too close to the side of the chamber.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Shaun41178||07-05-2000||08:07 PM||||Fiero Store is way over priced.  Cheapest way would be to go through the manufacturer direct.  That is what I did.  Valves cost $102 for all 12 and then $12 for shipping for a total of $114<P>1-800-SI-4VALVES<P>That is the number for the company.<P><BR>Hey I do Know something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
